          "viewing_task": "<ol><li><strong>[02:40] Recall:</strong> On what date and in what city did David Ben-Gurion proclaim the establishment of the State of Israel?</li><li><strong>[05:30] Explain:</strong> Explain how Britain's abrupt, uncoordinated withdrawal on 14 May 1948 transformed a localized civil conflict between communal militias into a full-scale regional interstate war.</li><li><strong>[08:15] Challenge:</strong> Evaluate the oral testimony of British and Arab veterans in this documentary. How do their retrospective accounts decades later challenge simplistic textbook summaries of the outbreak of the 1948 War?</li></ol>",
          "model_answer": "<ol><li><strong>Recall:</strong> David Ben-Gurion proclaimed the State of Israel on 14 May 1948 at the Tel Aviv Museum of Art.</li><li><strong>Explain:</strong> British forces withdrew without transferring authority, police archives, or key infrastructure to either the UN or local municipal authorities. This created an immediate vacuum of sovereignty: within hours of Israel's declaration, armies from five neighboring Arab states (Egypt, Transjordan, Syria, Lebanon, and Iraq) crossed the frontiers, escalating communal guerrilla skirmishes into a full-scale conventional interstate war.</li><li><strong>Challenge:</strong> Oral testimonies from soldiers and diplomats on both sides reveal that decisions were made amidst intense fog of war, acute weapon shortages, mutual panic, and deep political division within both the Arab League and Jewish factions. This shatters simplistic retrospective narratives that either side possessed a pre-planned, effortless military strategy, highlighting the chaotic, improvised reality of May 1948.</li></ol>"
