          "teacher_guidance": "Essential conceptual starter comparing the diametrically opposed historical memories of 1948: miraculous national rebirth vs catastrophic displacement. Recommended Watch Window: 00:00–04:45 • Lesson Phase: Starter Hook (0–5m). Tone Alert: Thoughtful historiographical comparison illustrating how the same military events in 1948 produced two completely irreconcilable national historical narratives.",
          "viewing_task": "<ol><li><strong>[01:10] Recall:</strong> What Arabic word is used by Palestinians to describe the 1948 catastrophe, and what Hebrew term is used by Israelis?</li><li><strong>[02:40] Explain:</strong> Explain why the 1948 war is interpreted simultaneously as an existential miracle of survival by Israelis and a catastrophe of dispossession by Palestinians.</li><li><strong>[04:15] Challenge:</strong> Analyze the concept of dual historical memory. How do these conflicting 1948 narratives continue to prevent diplomatic reconciliation over the 'Right of Return' today?</li></ol>",
