          "viewing_task": "<ol><li><strong>[02:00] Recall:</strong> Which European country supplied Israel with vital rifles, machine guns, and fighter aircraft during the first UN truce in June 1948?</li><li><strong>[03:50] Explain:</strong> Explain how unified military command under David Ben-Gurion and the dissolution of paramilitaries into the IDF gave Israel a decisive tactical advantage over divided Arab armies.</li><li><strong>[05:30] Challenge:</strong> Evaluate the presenter's discussion of Arab army strength in 1948. How do modern 'New Historians' (such as Avi Shlaim) challenge the traditional narrative that tiny Israel faced overwhelmingly superior Arab numbers?</li></ol>",
