          "model_answer": "<ol><li><strong>Recall:</strong> 'I have come bearing an olive branch and a freedom fighter's gun. Do not let the olive branch fall from my hand.'</li><li><strong>Explain:</strong> For twenty-six years, international diplomacy had treated Palestinians merely as displaced refugees requiring humanitarian aid (as in Resolution 242). Arafat's address forced the world to recognize Palestinians as a distinct nation with the inalienable right to sovereign self-determination.</li><li><strong>Challenge:</strong> Developing nations saw the PLO as a heroic liberation movement fighting Western imperialism, akin to the Algerian FLN or the Viet Cong. In contrast, Israel and the US pointed out that Arafat spoke with a gun holster on his hip shortly after PLO factions had carried out massacres at Munich and Ma'alot, arguing that granting him a global podium legitimized political violence against civilians.</li></ol>"
